<header><h1>The Empyrean</h1></header>
<article>
<h2 id="voidborn"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Empyrean#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Voidborn">Voidborn</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>This effect also applies outside the <b>Movement</b> step.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>The Empyrean player treats nebulae as nebulae and as anomalies for all other game purposes.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="aetherpassage"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Empyrean#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Aetherpassage">Aetherpassage</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Empyrean player does not decide to use this ability until after the other player has activated a system. Any deal made to use this ability before the system has been activated is non&ndash;binding.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="dark-whispers"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Empyrean#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Dark%20Whispers">Dark Whispers</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    </ol>

<h2 id="blood-pact"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Empyrean#Faction_Promissory_Notes:~:text=Blood%20Pact">Blood Pact</a> <sub>(Promissory Note)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Both players must cast at least one vote to trigger the additional votes.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol><li>If either player cannot vote on an agenda, then the additional votes will not trigger for that agenda.<sup>1</sup></li></ol>
    <li><i>Blood Pact</i> is returned when the system is activated, even if the active player will perform no hostile acts toward the Empyrean player this turn.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>Activating a system containing only the Empyrean player&rsquo;s structures will still cause <i>Blood Pact</i> to be returned.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If an effect other than activating a system during a tactical action places a command token in a system with the Empyrean player&rsquo;s units (for example, the primary ability of the <a href="/R_diplomacy"><i>Diplomacy</i></a> strategy card), this will not cause <i>Blood Pact</i> to be returned.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="dark-pact"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Empyrean#Faction_Promissory_Notes:~:text=Dark%20Pact">Dark Pact</a> <sub>(Promissory Note)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A player cannot have more commodities than their commodity value.<sup>1,3</sup></li>
    <li>If the Empyrean player plays a player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Trade_Agreement"><i>Trade Agreement</i></a> promissory note, this will count for that player giving the Empyrean player all their commodities.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>The trade goods gained from <i>Dark Pact</i> are gained simultaneously with the commodities transacted between the two players.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>As the trade goods from <i>Dark Pact</i> are gained simultaneously with any commodities and/or trade goods transacted, the <a href="/F_mentak">Mentak</a> player may only use their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Pillage"><sc>Pillage</sc></a> ability on each player once per <i>Dark Pact</i> transaction.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li><i>Dark Pact</i> is returned when the system is activated, even if the active player will perform no hostile acts toward the Empyrean player this turn.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>Activating a system containing only the Empyrean player&rsquo;s structures will still cause <i>Dark Pact</i> to be returned.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If an effect other than activating a system during a tactical action places a command token in a system with the Empyrean player&rsquo;s units (for example, the primary ability of the <a href="/R_diplomacy"><i>Diplomacy</i></a> strategy card), this will not cause <i>Dark Pact</i> to be returned.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="aetherstream"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Empyrean#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Aetherstream">Aetherstream</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Empyrean player does not decide to use this ability until after the other player has activated a system. Any deal made to use this ability before the system has been activated is non&ndash;binding.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>If a system is separated from an anomaly by the Empyrean player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Empyrean#Breakthrough:~:text=Void%20Tether">Void Tether</a> token, <i>Aetherstream</i> can only be used for that system if the Empyrean player allows it. This includes the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player using a copy of <i>Aetherstream</i>.<sup>6</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="voidwatch"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Empyrean#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Voidwatch">Voidwatch</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The active player chooses which promissory note they give the Empyrean player.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>Giving a promissory note because of <i>Voidwatch</i> is not resolving a transaction.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="dynamo"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Empyrean#Flagship:~:text=Dynamo">Dynamo</a> <sub>(Flagship)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A unit may only use its <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability once in each timing window, even if it is repaired.<sup>2,4</sup></li>
    <li>A unit that becomes damaged without using its <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability will not trigger this effect.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>A player may play a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Direct%20Hit"><i>Direct Hit</i></a> action card during the same timing window as this ability. If they do so, the ship is destroyed.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>Influence must be spent separately for each use of this ability. As such, any excess influence used to repair a ship is wasted, and cannot be used to repair a different ship.<sup>2,4</sup></li>
    <ol><li>As an example, The Dark may be exhausted to repair only one ship, not two.<sup>*</sup></li></ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="acamar"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Empyrean#Leaders:~:text=Acamar">Acamar</a> <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A system that contains a planet destroyed by the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Relics#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=Stellar%20Converter"><i>Stellar Converter</i></a> relic, and no other planets, is considered to contain no planets.<sup>4,6</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="xuange"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Empyrean#Leaders:~:text=Xuange">Xuange</a> <sub>(Commander)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>While the agenda phase allows a player to resolve transactions with all other players, it does not make that player neighbors with all other players.<sup>2,5</sup></li>
    <li>Any movement of ships can trigger this ability, not just movement during the <b>Move Ships</b> step of a tactical action.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If the Empyrean player becomes neighbors with all players when the final player moves ships into a system containing one of the Empyrean player&rsquo;s command tokens, Xuange will unlock, but the Empyrean player will not be able to resolve its ability from that movement.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>If the Empyrean player moves a ship into a system containing one of the <a href="/F_saar">Saar</a> player&rsquo;s Floating Factories, and no other ships, that <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Space_Dock:~:text=Floating%20Factory">Floating Factory</a> will be blockaded and destroyed before the Empyrean player can unlock Xuange. If the Empyrean and <a href="/F_saar">Saar</a> players are not neighbors in any other way, then Xuange will not unlock.<sup>2,6</sup></li>
    <li>Only the system in which a ship ends its movement is &ldquo;moved into&rdquo;; systems a ship moves through are not. As such, Xuange returns at most one command token for each movement.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="conservator-procyon"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Empyrean#Leaders:~:text=Conservator%20Procyon">Conservator Procyon</a> &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Empyrean#Leaders:~:text=Multiverse%20Shift">Multiverse Shift</a> <sub>(Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A system that contains a planet destroyed by the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Relics#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=Stellar%20Converter"><i>Stellar Converter</i></a> relic, and no other planets, is considered to contain no planets.<sup>4,6</sup></li>
    <li>If The Fracture is in play when the Empyrean player resolves <i>Multiverse Shift</i>, frontier tokens will be placed in the systems in The Fracture that do not contain a planet.<sup>2,6</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="watcher"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Empyrean#Mech:~:text=Watcher">Watcher</a> <sub>(Mech)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>This effect may cancel a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Sabotage"><i>Sabotage</i></a> action card.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>The Watcher must be adjacent to the other player&rsquo;s units during the timing window when the action card is played in order to cancel it.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol><li>In particular, if an action card is played &ldquo;when/after you activate a system&rdquo; or similar, then the Watcher must be adjacent before any ships move during that tactical action.<sup>*</sup></li></ol>
    <li>If an action card is canceled by a Watcher, no costs are paid.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>A player playing an action card announces the following before a Watcher may be triggered:<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li>Any targeted planets, system, units, players, cards, outcomes, and/or other such objects.<sup>1,2,5</sup></li>
        <li>The value of any variable cost to be paid.<sup>5</sup></li>
    </ol>
    <li>Any dice are rolled and any cards are drawn only after the Empyrean player has declined to remove a Watcher.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If an action card instructs a player to research a technology, that player need not announce what technology they are researching until the Empyrean player has declined to remove a Watcher.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If an action card is played that will have an effect later, such as a rider, that card may only be canceled by a Watcher when it is originally played.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If the action card that was canceled by a Watcher was to be used to perform a component action, the active player must perform a different action, or pass.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <ol><li>If the component action was to be the second action the active player was to perform on their turn, through an effect such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Fleet_Logistics"><i>Fleet Logistics</i></a> technology, the active player may end their turn without performing a second action and without passing.<sup>2</sup></li></ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="void-tether"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Empyrean#Breakthrough:~:text=Void%20Tether">Void Tether</a> <sub>(Breakthrough)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Other players treat the systems that share the border with the Void Tether token as not being adjacent for all game effects, even if both systems contain matching <a href="/R_wormholes">wormholes</a>. The Empyrean player continues to treat them as adjacent.<sup>6</sup></li>
    <ol><li>If the Empyrean player has units or controls a planet in one of the systems, they will be neighbors with any player with units or controlling a planet in the other, and vice versa.<sup>6</sup></li></ol>
    <li>If the Empyrean player is eliminated, <i>Void Tether</i> remains in play, and the Void Tether tokens continue to function.<sup>6</sup></li>
    </ol>
</article>
